ios: music lets go of the buffers it has played

tinymidipcm renders a whole song ahead (about 19 times real time) into AudioBuffers of about 4.6 s and kept every one
of them in bufferSources until the next song: 176 KB a second of music, 33 MB for a median song. A source now leaves
bufferSources once it has ended (onended, which fires for stopped sources too), so its buffer can be collected.
stop() has only the sources still to play to stop, as stopping an ended one did nothing, and its gain steps still
follow whether a buffer was flushed since the last stop() (`flushed`, what bufferSources.length said).

The rendered chunks are copied from the wasm heap straight into one accumulator kept from chunk to chunk (grown only
when a chunk does not fit), instead of a new Uint8Array per chunk and a new, longer Float32Array per concatenation:
about 190 MB of garbage per song start. Chunks rendered after a stop() are not kept: the stop() before the next
start() dropped them unplayed, and after a stop() with no next song (Music off, logout) the render runs on to the
song's end.

The render loop and its timing, the synthesizer, and every buffer's samples and start time are as before.

